Moonsilence wrote:
> What are the keys to success in NetHack?

Patience. Play only if you are relaxed and good mood.
Awareness that you don't play against a timer. Play slow.
Reflection about the situation and causes of your deaths.
Learning; don't do things again if they killed you.
Have a plan! (What is the next milestone? What do I lack
for the current phase of the game? Where can I get that,
while considering my health/power and actual equipment.)

> [...], and consequently forget a portion of acquired
> knowlegde over time as a result.

Knowledge is the lesser part of the success story, IMO.

> The learning curve is extremly shallow in my opinion.

(Hmm.. - rethink about that ;-)

> I never got far in 
> the game. Quite soon the monsters just get too tough/dangerous for me. 
> That zoo at Sokoban's end! Those Yetis in the Rogue Level! Gees! Yikes!

Add the concept of fleeing to your set of tactics!
Get some help, get pets.
Engrave the E-word early and often.
Avoid melee if you can handle things from distance.
Have escape means at hand (teleport scrolls from niches).

